From: Ze contributors
Subject: [PATCH] pppoe: expose nonce-fenced resource ownership and reconciliation

Keep every adopted message layout and CRC unchanged. Add Ze-only APIs whose
process nonce and caller owner token distinguish a retry from a foreign
replacement after a lost receipt. Native session tokens clear on allocation
and original reconfiguration. Reciprocal CP map tokens use a fixed 4096-slot
table and clear on original writes or interface removal/reuse.

Read exact named policer indices and allocated directional slots without
inferring an index from dump order. Cold policer receipts carry independent
session and object lifetime tokens; legacy add, update and delete invalidate
them without enlarging the 64-byte packet-path policer structure. Guard slot
writes by the actual session
owner, expected binding and derived owned name; repeated enables do not stack
features and removal requires the corresponding arcs to be fenced first.
Initialize untouched policer slots to ~0 because pool index zero is valid.

Guard route, protocol/policer feature, MTU, admin and family-table mutations
inside their serialized native handlers. Guard policer create/update/delete
by native receipt metadata, exact index and all directional slots. Repeated
updates retain buckets/counters; an unbound orphan can be deleted without
touching the old interface. A removed CP interface can confirm map absence
only when both cells and its ownership record are absent. Bounded native
route receipts remove exact IPv4/IPv6 paths before session/interface release.
Session retirement fences receive/policer arcs and unlinks native slots before
a hidden software index can be reused, retaining policer object receipts.

Delete a manual session from its exact native record even after its learned
link disappears. A refused duplicate add no longer moves its hash entry.
An unowned original session never lends its undecidable FIB family to the
IPv4 ownership reply. The existing lab option adds a 55-case native regression
of these producers, including a foreign IPv6 FIB without an IPv4 counterpart.
Intrinsic creation suppresses the stock implicit peer route; owned shared-prefix
paths coexist and exact withdrawal preserves other owners and sources.

Upstream: https://github.com/FDio/vpp at cbba0451bb0af02a3ab8e163f6f99062782258e6
Applies after the unchanged five VyOS diffs and Ze patches 0098 through 0102.

